llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: operator new's result is nonnull only at a new-expression (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a null test of operator new's
result. r256787 (Philip Reames, 2016-01-04, "[MemoryBuiltins] Remove
isOperatorNewLike by consolidating non-null inference handling", first
release LLVM 3.8) replaced isKnownNonNull's isOperatorNewLikeFn test,
which held only where the call may be the builtin (a new-expression; a
direct call of the nobuiltin declaration did not qualify), with a
nonnull return attribute that InferFunctionAttrs puts on the
declaration of _Znwj/_Znwm/_Znaj/_Znam, so every call, direct or not,
loses its null test. The game region keeps `test rax, rax` after 156
calls of _Znwm, every one branching to _Xbad_alloc (130 of them the
std::function copy and move slots, whose source tests the pointer), a
form the unpatched line cannot emit; 2,110 calls are untested (rounds
147A and 149B). This patch restores the
pre-r256787 rule: no nonnull on the declaration, and isKnownNonNull
treats a non-nobuiltin call of the four one-argument operator news as
nonnull (by name, as TargetLibraryInfo names them on this target).

--- a/lib/Analysis/ValueTracking.cpp
+++ b/lib/Analysis/ValueTracking.cpp
@@ -3385,9 +3385,19 @@
   if (const LoadInst *LI = dyn_cast<LoadInst>(V))
     return LI->getMetadata(LLVMContext::MD_nonnull);
 
-  if (auto CS = ImmutableCallSite(V))
+  if (auto CS = ImmutableCallSite(V)) {
     if (CS.isReturnNonNull())
       return true;
+    // PS4: operator new never returns null where the call may be treated as
+    // the builtin (a new-expression), as isOperatorNewLikeFn gave it before
+    // r256787 (LLVM 3.8).
+    if (!CS.isNoBuiltin())
+      if (const Function *F = CS.getCalledFunction())
+        if (F->getFunctionType()->getNumParams() == 1 &&
+            (F->getName() == "_Znwj" || F->getName() == "_Znwm" ||
+             F->getName() == "_Znaj" || F->getName() == "_Znam"))
+          return true;
+  }
 
   return false;
 }
--- a/lib/Transforms/Utils/BuildLibCalls.cpp
+++ b/lib/Transforms/Utils/BuildLibCalls.cpp
@@ -682,8 +682,9 @@
   case LibFunc::msvc_new_longlong: // new(unsigned long long)
   case LibFunc::msvc_new_array_int: // new[](unsigned int)
   case LibFunc::msvc_new_array_longlong: // new[](unsigned long long)
-    // Operator new always returns a nonnull noalias pointer
-    Changed |= setNonNull(F, AttributeSet::ReturnIndex);
+    // PS4: no nonnull on the declaration (r256787, 2016-01-04, LLVM 3.8):
+    // a direct call of operator new keeps its null test; a new-expression's
+    // result is known nonnull in isKnownNonNull, as before that change.
     Changed |= setDoesNotAlias(F, AttributeSet::ReturnIndex);
     return Changed;
   //TODO: add LibFunc entries for:
